# Drafted by Gemini (R20), edited. R20: inside the dovecote: Golub before the fight, her stashed secrets, and home to roost.

~ golub
Narrator: At the north end of the roost sits a platform of matted straw and cloth before four drafty windows. Perched atop it, the pigeon hag preens her slick grey feathers with crooked fingers.
golub_graygullet [sly]: Coo, what a frightful fuss you made climbing up to my parlor. I do hope the mud on your boots was worth playing the fool for me.
-> menu

~ menu
* [Insight DC 15] Watch the way she preens. -> vain | vain_missed
* Tell her we are ending this here. -> attack
* Say nothing and draw our weapons. -> attack
* Back quietly down the ladder. -> END

~ vain
set rk_golub_vain
Narrator: She cannot keep her wings still for a heartbeat, angling her chin toward the light with every breath. She is starving for praise, so bloated with vanity that a sharp compliment would strike her harder than iron.
-> menu
~ vain_missed
Narrator: The reek of wet feathers and old tallow presses in on your throat. Her presence fills the rafters, and you cannot quite find her measure.
-> menu

~ attack
set rk_golub_started
golub_graygullet [angry]: You dare track filth into my nest and bares your teeth at me? Nobody climbs into Golub's roost and walks back down!
Narrator: The timbers groan as the whole building heaves up on its scaly legs and the floor pitches beneath your boots. Hundreds of grey pigeons erupt from the cubbies in a blinding, beating storm.
combat rk_golub

~ cubbies
Narrator: Every wooden cubby along the wall is crammed with stolen letters, diaries, and folded scraps of parchment. Each bundle bears a villager's name in a neat, spidery hand, alongside the price they paid to keep it dark.
* Read through every bundle. -> read
* Leave the secrets where they lie. -> END
~ read
set golub_secrets_read
set cult_proof_randall
set cult_proof_alda
set cult_proof_baltus
set cult_proof_gaston
set cult_proof_howie
Narrator: An hour passes in the rustle of dry paper and dusty down. By the last page, you know which altars your neighbours truly keep, and which of them kneel in the dark to the antlered hare.
-> END

~ home_to_roost
cutscene rk_home_to_roost
Narrator: With a final, hollow shudder, the great bird legs fold beneath the floor and the shingled wings tuck tight into the thatch. The dovecote drops to the earth with a heavy thump that shakes the dust from the beams, settled for good.
cutscene rk_home_to_roost_2
Narrator: Over in the scattered straw lies the pudgy little spy, still and cold. His bald head rests among the husks, one waxen human ear turned up toward the quiet rafters.
cutscene rk_home_to_roost_3
Narrator: Down in the lanes of Wickermoor, neighbours stand blinking in the pale gloom like sleepers waking from a fever. Up on a porch, someone clears their throat and hangs the first bright strand of festival bunting.
cutscene end
set golub_dead
quest roving_rookery done
xp milestone
if quest.quiet_door == asked
quest quiet_door moot
endif
if quest.jury_of_pigeons == asked
quest jury_of_pigeons moot
endif
if quest.forms_for_the_end == asked
quest forms_for_the_end moot
endif
if quest.forms_for_the_end == stamped
quest forms_for_the_end moot
endif
if quest.powder_keg_ledger == asked
quest powder_keg_ledger moot
endif
Narrator: The charm lifts from the valley like a long held breath finally let go. Up on the gables, the grey birds go back to being only pigeons, and a very long night is nearly done.
-> END
